  "title": "Chapter 35: Rivers of India",
  "order": 36,
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "iap6wln",
      "content": "Rivers are vital natural resources in India. They provide water for irrigation, drinking, transportation, fisheries, and hydroelectric power generation. Indian rivers also play an important role in agriculture, settlement patterns, and cultural traditions. The river systems of India are broadly divided into Himalayan rivers and Peninsular rivers."
    },
